{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FLhsa2aYn7SfZHe5CW3K3M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` provides shared libraries (sys, format, testutils), `magefiles/` drives orchestration. Differential testing in `pkg/testutils/` compares Go binary output byte-for-byte against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 02.2 have specs implemented. Release 05.0 (\"text stream transforms\": echo, tac, nl, fold) is the current target. Echo was just implemented (commit `2d0350f`). Tac, nl, and fold remain.\n\n**Current release:** 05.0. Next utility in canonical order: **tac**.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nEcho is done (per git history). Tac is next in the rel05.0 use case list. It has no pkg/ dependencies beyond testutils and sys (SIGPIPE handler). It's a standalone utility — no blockers.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/tac: implement tac utility (prd-tac R1-R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd-tac.yaml (all requirements and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.0-uc002-tac.yaml (end-to-end execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.0.yaml (tac test cases)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section -- differential testing pattern, SIGPIPE handling)\n      - cmd/echo/main.go (reference for cmd/ utility structure and patterns in this release)\n      - cmd/echo/echo_test.go (reference for differential test structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/tac/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: tac utility implementation -- reverse concatenation of files\n      - path: cmd/tac/tac_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gtac reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement the tac command that concatenates and prints files in reverse,\n          line by line (last line first), per prd-tac. When no file arguments are\n          given or when \"-\" is specified, read from stdin. Write reversed output\n          to stdout.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement the -s/--separator flag per prd-tac. Use the given string as\n          the record separator instead of newline. By default the separator is\n          attached after each record (trailing); with -b/--before, attach it\n          before each record (leading).\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement the -b/--before flag per prd-tac. When set, the separator is\n          attached before each record instead of after.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement the -r/--regex flag per prd-tac. When set, treat the separator\n          string as a Go regular expression (regexp package). If the regex is\n          invalid, print a diagnostic to stderr and exit with status 1.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per the\n          ARCHITECTURE shared_protocols for SIGPIPE handling.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Follow the differential testing pattern from ARCHITECTURE shared_protocols.\n          Use testutils.BuildBinary to compile the Go binary and exec.LookPath for\n          \"gtac\" as the reference binary. Call t.Skip if gtac is not found.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Use --version flag detection to print version and exit 0, matching the\n          pattern used in cmd/echo and other utilities in this project.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Read entire file content into memory before reversing. tac requires\n          backward traversal of the input, so streaming is not feasible. Use\n          os.ReadAll for stdin and os.ReadFile for file arguments.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/tac/main.go compiles with no errors or lint warnings under golangci-lint.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"tac with no arguments reads stdin and prints lines in reverse order.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"tac with file arguments concatenates files and prints all lines in reverse.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"tac -s SEP splits on the given separator string and reverses records.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"tac -b attaches the separator before each record instead of after.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"tac -r treats the separator as a regular expression.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/tac/ passes with gtac as the reference binary.\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when gtac is not in PATH.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27551,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27551},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00db2a95-accc-41d3-9843-a9c03f94a098","uuid":"e230060d-d0d3-4d1a-be95-d4991e1a954e"}
